35,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I'm concerned. The development budget is smaller than we thought, and off-site work brings in no revenue. We must prioritize on-site programs.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shion,,"Interestingly, the call-back trial actually worked. Readmissions dropped by twenty percent. It's a shame we buried it. We need results, not just ""plans.""","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Midori,,I'm very worried. Our ward nursing vacancies are rising and we're relying too much on agency staff. We cannot add more pressure to the wards.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Guys, it's worse than I thought. The parking is full by 11 AM and the booking system is a disaster! It doesn't even record unscheduled work.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shizue,,I've found something quite sad. A previous joint clinic failed because no one would take responsibility for the budget or the rota. We must be careful.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shion, if the call-back trial was off-site, it might be a financial drain. We need a program that pays for itself.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, a twenty percent drop in readmissions saves the hospital far more in penalties and bed-blocking than a few phone calls cost. Logic, please.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, but who makes those calls? If it's the ward nurses, they're already exhausted. We can't just add ""more calls"" to a vacant post.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Kenji,,And where do these patients go if they need a follow-up? The rooms are already full by mid-morning. We'll have people waiting in the halls!,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, you are right to worry. I also saw that data agreements with outside surgeries take over a year to sign. We can't rely on outside help.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"If we can't use outside help and we can't afford off-site work, we must find a program that uses existing on-site space efficiently.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shion,,"Efficiency is a buzzword. I'm talking about patient outcomes. If a program has a proven track record of reducing readmissions, that is the only logical choice.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Midori,,"I noticed the midwifery rota actually has some slack. If we can find a program that utilizes that capacity instead of the wards, I'd be supportive.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"But the booking system is a black hole! If we start a program that isn't strictly ""named slots,"" we won't even know if it's being used.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shizue,,Let's please make sure that whoever is in charge of the program actually signs a formal agreement. I don't want another clinic to collapse.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
